Yes, if the odds of finding a WOW on level 1 are 1/4000, the odds of
finding exactly one WOW after 4000 games is 50%.  The odds of finding at
least 1 are 63% (at least what those other two people posted looked right).

I guess that means that 13% of the time you'll find more that one WOW after
playing 4000 games.  However, all that is based on an assumption that the
odds are 1/4000.  Now, does anyone want to figure out the actual probability 
for a WOW to appear on level 1?

To figure this out, you'd figure two things: 
 a) the average number of items created on level 1
 b) the chances that a given item is a WOW

a) is probably tougher (You'd have to figure out the average number of 
rooms, the average size of room, the average number of items per room, 
...) to calculate directly from the code, but it could be estimated
by running a few games.  I'll start 4 games and quaff potions of object
detection.  On these four tries I see 9, 6, 12, and 11 objects (ignoring
boulders in halls and gold in vaults), for an average of 9.5 (someone 
with more patience than me could try a bigger sample).

I'll ignore chests which may contain WOW, and just look at the odds of a 
WOW just lying on the floor.  At first glance, it looks like (for normal 
levels like 1) 4% of objects created are wands, and 0.5% of wands created 
are WOW.  This would mean that 1/5000 objects is a WOW.  Using the 9.5 
number, that would mean there is a 1/526 chance that level 1 contains a 
WOW.  This seems way too frequent, but that's the way it looks to me.
